  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:ctx-notes"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:BoundedContext"/><rdfs:label>Notes</rdfs:label></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:file-src-notes-create-py"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:CodeFile"/><rdfs:label>src/notes/create.py</rdfs:label></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:file-src-notes-note-py"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:CodeFile"/><rdfs:label>src/notes/note.py</rdfs:label></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:AC-N-001"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Criterion"/><rdfs:label>Given a title and a body, when the author saves, then the note is stored with an id and both timestamps.</rdfs:label><vb:criterionOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-001"/><vb:satisfiesRequirement rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:AC-N-002"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Criterion"/><rdfs:label>Given an empty or blank body, when the author saves, then nothing is stored and the reason names the body.</rdfs:label><vb:criterionOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-001"/><vb:satisfiesRequirement rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:AC-N-003"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Criterion"/><rdfs:label>Given a body over 100 KB, when the author saves, then nothing is stored and the reason gives the limit.</rdfs:label><vb:criterionOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-001"/><vb:satisfiesRequirement rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:REQ-NFR-002"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:AC-N-004"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Criterion"/><rdfs:label>Given a saved note, when the author asks for it by id, then the title, body and timestamps are returned unchanged.</rdfs:label><vb:criterionOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-002"/><vb:satisfiesRequirement rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-002"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:AC-N-005"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Criterion"/><rdfs:label>Given an id that was never issued, when the author asks for it, then the system reports that no such note exists.</rdfs:label><vb:criterionOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-002"/><vb:satisfiesRequirement rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-002"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:AC-N-006"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Criterion"/><rdfs:label>TBD: Given (state), when (action), then (observable outcome).</rdfs:label><vb:criterionOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-003"/><vb:satisfiesRequirement rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-003"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:STK-PRB-001"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Problem"/><rdfs:label>Small pieces of text (shopping lists, meeting points, half ideas) end up scattered across files and chats.</rdfs:label></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:STK-PRB-002"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Problem"/><rdfs:label>Once there are many notes, finding one means opening them all.</rdfs:label></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:STK-PRB-003"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Problem"/><rdfs:label>A note saved over by mistake loses what it said before.</rdfs:label></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-001"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Request"/><rdfs:label>I want to keep notes: write one, read it later, and fix it when I got something wrong.</rdfs:label><vb:concernsProblem rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-PRB-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-002"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Request"/><rdfs:label>When I have a lot of notes I want to find the one I mean without opening them all.</rdfs:label><vb:concernsProblem rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-PRB-002"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-001"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Requirement"/><rdfs:label>The system shall let the author create a note from a body and an optional title.</rdfs:label><vb:satisfiesRequest rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-002"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Requirement"/><rdfs:label>The system shall let the author read a saved note by its id.</rdfs:label><vb:satisfiesRequest rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:REQ-FR-003"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Requirement"/><rdfs:label>The system shall let the author edit the title or body of a saved note.</rdfs:label><vb:satisfiesRequest rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:REQ-NFR-001"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Requirement"/><rdfs:label>Durability: A saved note is still there after the application restarts.</rdfs:label><vb:satisfiesRequest rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:REQ-NFR-002"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Requirement"/><rdfs:label>Input limits: A note body is at most 100 KB, so one note cannot exhaust memory.</rdfs:label><vb:satisfiesRequest rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:STK-REQ-001"/></rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:vbench:project:STP-N-001"><rdf:type rdf:resource="urn:vbench:method:Step"/><rdfs:label>create_note(title, body)</rdfs:label><vb:stepDrivenBy rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:file-tests-test-create-note-py"/><vb:stepOf rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:UC-N-001"/><vb:stepRealisedIn rdf:resource="urn:vbench:project:file-src-notes-create-py"/><vb:planned rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">false</vb:planned></rdf:Description>
